---
title: Rigid Body Work-Precision Diagrams
author: Chris Rackauckas
---

```julia
using OrdinaryDiffEq, ParameterizedFunctions, ODEInterfaceDiffEq, LSODA,
      Sundials, DiffEqDevTools, StaticArrays, OrdinaryDiffEqSIMDRK, IRKGaussLegendre
using OrdinaryDiffEqAdamsBashforthMoulton, OrdinaryDiffEqExtrapolation, OrdinaryDiffEqHighOrderRK, OrdinaryDiffEqLowOrderRK
using SciMLLogging

k(t) = 0.25*sin(t)^2

g = @ode_def RigidBody begin
    dy1 = I₁*y2*y3
    dy2 = I₂*y1*y3
    dy3 = I₃*y1*y2 + k(t)
end I₁ I₂ I₃

p = SA[-2.0, 1.25, -0.5]
prob = ODEProblem{true, SciMLBase.FullSpecialize}(g, [1.0; 0.0; 0.9], (0.0, 10.0), p)
probstatic = ODEProblem{false}(g, SA[1.0; 0.0; 0.9], (0.0, 10.0), p)

abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (6:13)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (3:10);
sol_plot = solve(prob, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14)
sol_endpoint = solve(prob, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14, save_everystep = false, dense = false)
sol2_endpoint = solve(probstatic, Vern7(), abstol = 1/10^14, reltol = 1/10^14, save_everystep = false, dense = false)
probs = [prob, probstatic]
test_sol = [sol_endpoint, sol2_endpoint];
using Plots;
gr()
include(joinpath(@__DIR__, "..", "workprecision_table.jl"))

const RIGID_BODY_ERROR_FLOOR = 1.0e-14
const RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_IRKGL_TAGS = [:irkgl, :implicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:ordinarydiffeq, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS = [:odeinterface, :extrapolation, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_SUNDIALS_RK_TAGS = [:sundials, :explicit_rk, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_SUNDIALS_MULTISTEP_TAGS = [:sundials, :adams, :multistep, :nonstiff]
const RIGID_BODY_LSODA_TAGS = [:lsoda, :multistep, :nonstiff]
```

Each sweep requests only the endpoint error with `error_estimates = [:final]` and
attaches solver metadata tags to the results. The table accompanying each existing
work-precision figure reports the best endpoint error, that point's timing,
right-hand-side calls, accepted steps, and the computed refinement rate over mean
accepted step sizes. The existing solvers are adaptive, so the fixed-step observed
order is unavailable. Rate calculations exclude errors at or below `1e-14`, the
tolerance used to construct each numerical endpoint reference; an em dash means the
grid did not resolve a rate or a counter is unavailable. The plotted reference
trajectory retains dense output because the figure consumes it.

```julia
plot(sol_plot)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP5(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode45()) # fails
          Dict(:alg=>dopri5(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)]
low_order_setups = setups
low_order_abstols = abstols
low_order_reltols = reltols
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = true, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100, maxiters = 10000)
low_order_wp = wp
print_work_table(wp, RIGID_BODY_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

The DifferentialEquations.jl algorithms once again pull ahead. `dopri5` does surprisingly badly in this test. ODE.jl is not part of this benchmark's environment; its setups are left commented out for reference.

## Higher Order

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>DP8(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>dop853(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_RK_TAGS)
          #Dict(:alg=>ode78()) # fails
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = false), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>IRKGL16(simd = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_IRKGL_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern6(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100, maxiters = 1000)
print_work_table(wp, RIGID_BODY_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern7(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern8(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>odex(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>CVODE_Adams(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_SUNDIALS_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>lsoda(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_LSODA_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ddeabm(), :tags=>[RIGID_BODY_ODEINTERFACE_MULTISTEP_TAGS..., :accepted_steps_unavailable])
          Dict(:alg=>ARKODE(Sundials.Explicit(), order = 6), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_SUNDIALS_RK_TAGS)]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, numruns = 100, maxiters = 1000)
print_work_table(wp, RIGID_BODY_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

## Comparison with Non-RK methods

Now let's test Tsit5 and Vern9 against parallel extrapolation methods and an
Adams-Bashforth-Moulton:

```julia
abstols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (8:13)
reltols = 1.0 ./ 10.0 .^ (8:13)
setups = [Dict(:alg=>Tsit5(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>VCABM(), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>Vern9(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_RK_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>VCABM(), :prob_choice => 2, :tags=>RIGID_BODY_MULTISTEP_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>AitkenNeville(min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointDeuflhard(
              min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)]
solnames = ["Tsit5", "Vern9", "VCABM", "Vern9 Static", "VCABM Static",
    "AitkenNeville", "Midpoint Deuflhard", "Midpoint Hairer Wanner"]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(
    probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, names = solnames, error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
print_work_table(wp, RIGID_BODY_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointDeuflhard(
              min_order = 1, max_order = 9, init_order = 9, threading = false), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = false), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4,
              sequence = :romberg, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4,
              sequence = :bulirsch, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)]
solnames = ["Deuflhard", "No threads", "standard", "Romberg", "Bulirsch"]
wp = WorkPrecisionSet(
    probs, abstols, reltols, setups; appxsol = test_sol, names = solnames, error_estimates = [:final],
    save_everystep = false, verbose = SciMLLogging.None(), numruns = 100)
print_work_table(wp, RIGID_BODY_ERROR_FLOOR)
plot(wp)
```

```julia
setups = [Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 10, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
              min_order = 2, max_order = 11, init_order = 4, threading = true), :tags=>RIGID_BODY_EXTRAPOLATION_TAGS)
          Dict(:alg=>ExtrapolationMidpointHairerWanner(
